frac{{a}_{n-1}}{2}+\\frac{{a}_{n-2}}{3}-4.$\n\n- The largest index difference between ${a}_{n}$ and the preceding terms ${a}_{n-1}$ and ${a}_{n-2}$ in the relation is $2.$ So, the relation has order $2.$\n\n- The previous terms ${a}_{n-1}$ and ${a}_{n-2}$ occur only in the first power and their  coefficients are constants. So, the relation is linear.\n\n- The relation is linear, and the forcing function $g(n)=-4$ is nonzero. So, the relation is inhomogeneous.\n\nTherefore, the recurrence relation ${a}_{n}$ has order\n$2,$\nis\n$\\text{linear},$\nand is\n$\\text{inhomogeneous}.$" 13194139534642 true] [17592186300745 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300746 13194139534642 true] [17592186300745 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300747 13194139534642 true] [17592186300745 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300748 13194139534642 true] [17592186300745 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139534642 true] [17592186300745 1041 "field-1" 13194139534642 true] [17592186300745 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300747 13194139534642 true] [17592186300745 1110 #uuid "d9600b00-1da4-5f71-8362-133281a7fdbe" 13194139534642 true] [17592186300746 1034 "3" 13194139534642 true] [17592186300746 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534642 true] [17592186300746 1111 #uuid "21f6bead-4306-5ced-b37f-0a8a83f20b5a" 13194139534642 true] [17592186300747 1034 "2" 13194139534642 true] [17592186300747 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534642 true] [17592186300747 1111 #uuid "bcaceabd-e8d3-596b-9a56-33eefe1d4661" 13194139534642 true] [17592186300748 1034 "1" 13194139534642 true] [17592186300748 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534642 true] [17592186300748 1111 #uuid "52d1aa58-97fb-55ad-a869-07988b49bac4" 13194139534642 true] [17592186300749 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300750 13194139534642 true] [17592186300749 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300751 13194139534642 true] [17592186300749 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139534642 true] [17592186300749 1041 "field-2" 13194139534642 true] [17592186300749 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300750 13194139534642 true] [1759218630