e relations are first-order?\n\n- ${a}_{n}={a}_{n-1}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}$\n- ${b}_{n}=3{b}_{n-2}$\n- ${c}_{n}=\\frac{{c}_{n-1}}{3}-2{c}_{n-3}$" 13194139534642 true] [17592186300780 1113 #uuid "21a536a7-eaf5-542f-8447-68faf609e75b" 13194139534642 true] [17592186300780 1145 "The order of a recurrence relation is the largest index difference between ${a}_{n}$ and the preceding terms in the relation.\n\nLet's examine each recurrence relation in turn.\n\n- The largest index difference between ${a}_{n}$ and the preceding term ${a}_{n-1}$ in the relation is $1.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $1.$\n\n- The largest index difference between ${b}_{n}$ and the preceding terms ${b}_{n-1}$ and ${b}_{n-2}$ in the relation is $2.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $2.$\n\n- The largest index difference between ${c}_{n}$ and the preceding terms ${c}_{n-1}$ and ${c}_{n-3}$ in the relation is $3.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534642 true] [17592186300781 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300782 13194139534642 true] [17592186300781 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300783 13194139534642 true] [17592186300781 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300784 13194139534642 true] [17592186300781 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300785 13194139534642 true] [17592186300781 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300786 13194139534642 true] [17592186300781 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534642 true] [17592186300781 1041 "selection" 13194139534642 true] [17592186300781 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300784 13194139534642 true] [17592186300781 1110 #uuid "2bf99fd1-7c68-5365-8973-de32cc1695e3" 13194139534642 true] [17592186300782 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534642 true] [17592186300782 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534642 true] [17592186300782 1111 #uuid "d38f5400-d221-566e-ba0f-6a50498ca8ff" 13194139534642 true] [17592186300783 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534642 true] [17592186300783 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534642 true] [17592186300783 1111 #uuid "afe60291-e78e-